Here is an Apex trigger that prevents duplicate Account names on insert and update:

```apex
trigger PreventDuplicateAccount on Account (before insert, before update) {
    Set<String> names = new Set<String>();
    for (Account a : Trigger.new) {
        if (a.Name != null) {
            names.add(a.Name.toLowerCase());
        }
    }

    List<Account> existing = [
        SELECT Id, Name FROM Account
        WHERE Name IN :names
        AND Id NOT IN :Trigger.newMap.keySet()
    ];

    Map<String, Account> nameMap = new Map<String, Account>();
    for (Account a : existing) {
        nameMap.put(a.Name.toLowerCase(), a);
    }

    for (Account a : Trigger.new) {
        if (a.Name != null && nameMap.containsKey(a.Name.toLowerCase())) {
            a.Name.addError('An account with this name already exists.');
        }
    }
}
```

Key points: this trigger is bulkified (processes all records in a single SOQL query), excludes the current record on update via `Trigger.newMap.keySet()`, and uses `addError()` to block the save.
